 "id": "zenodo:18462868",
 "title": "Raman microscopy of live Schizosaccharomyces pombe yeast",
 "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/18462868",
 "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.18462868",
 "description": "<p>We acquired coherent Raman microscopy data on fission yeast<em> Schizosaccharomyces pombe</em> (wild-type) and two mutants, dea2 and pdf1. Our aim was to collect spatially resolved biochemical data on living yeast cells. The image preview (rgb_overlay_large.png) is a composite of two single-wavenumber SRS acquisitions, taken at 2,850 (green) and 2,937 cm&minus;1 (blue).&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This record contains the raw LIF files and metadata in JSON and CSV format. This release accompanies the pub <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.57844/arcadia-xemg-d6wv\">\"Coherent Raman imaging of live, unfixed Schizosaccharomyces pombe and mutants dea2 and pdf1\"</a>, and the GitHub repository for visualizing the dataset and exporting images and metadata is <a href=\"https://github.com/Arcadia-Science/2026-spombe-dataset\">here</a>.&nbsp;</p>",
 "found_by_keywords": [
  "science"
 ],
